    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de929f48_02b9b6e8",
        "filename": "drivers/android/bpf/bpf_fd_loader.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T04:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the premises is that the bpf programs must be loaded from a dm_verity partition. Why not enforce this check here?",
      "revId": "01aa9adf2f9634f68cff53f46e713bdeb9c7cbb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "00a19c1b_73074f50",
        "filename": "drivers/android/bpf/bpf_fd_loader.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 249,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-02T01:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is already here! This is happening via the LSM hook for `security_kernel_read_file` called within `kernel_read_file`. SELinux will kick in and make sure that the right permission has been granted to \"load this file as a kernel module\". \n\nEnforcing on the policy side give us more flexibility.",
      "parentUuid": "de929f48_02b9b6e8",
      "revId": "01aa9adf2f9634f68cff53f46e713bdeb9c7cbb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe6c0b2e_2522e660",
        "filename": "drivers/android/bpf/bpf_fd_loader.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T04:23:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t we want a different `kernel_read_file_id`? Seems like overloading the `module` id could be limiting.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "01aa9adf2f9634f68cff53f46e713bdeb9c7cbb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1cba3f6_8ecd2860",
        "filename": "drivers/android/bpf/bpf_fd_loader.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 1561651
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-02T01:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s a trade-off. The initial PoC had a different id. Jeff suggested reusing `module` as we are treating both equally.\n\nCons of introducing a new id:\n- This is part of the kernel API, we would need to pick something that won\u0027t conflict with any upstream addition (https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/common/+/android-mainline:include/linux/kernel_read_file.h;l\u003d18;drc\u003d4c269eab9889712dd561ecf3f0302c183d73e473). Is there any elegant way to add an enum without making future merge painful?\n- The SELinux policy for kernel modules has been shipped with the platform for a while. If we decide to do any kind of backporting, reusing the existing policy allows us to piggy back on it.\n\nI can\u0027t think of any sufficient reason why we would want a different id, but if you have a preference here, I\u0027m ok to go down that path.",
      "parentUuid": "fe6c0b2e_2522e660",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "01aa9adf2f9634f68cff53f46e713bdeb9c7cbb7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
